        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 10</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="56" ed="#liebermann"/>XI. Gif mon hæme mid twelfhyndes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.1"/> monnes wife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.2"/>, hundtwelftig scill. gebete ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.3"/> were; syxhyndum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.4"/> men<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.star"/> hundteontig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.5"/> scill. gebete; cierliscum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.6"/> men feowertig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.7"/> scill. gebete.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.8"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.star2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="56" ed="#liebermann"/>XI. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.1-2"/> hæme mid XIIhyndes monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.1-2"/> wife, CXX scll' gebete (man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.2-2"/>) þam were; syxhyndum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.3-2"/> men C scill' gebete; cyrliscum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.4-2"/> men XL scll' gebete.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.2-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Be hæmedðingu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Gif mon hæme mid twelfhyndes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.1-4"/> mannes wífe, hundtwelftig scill' g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>bete man were. Syxhyndu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.1-4"/></hi> m<hi rend="italic">en</hi> hundteontigon scyll' g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>bete. Ceorliscu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> m<hi rend="italic">en</hi> feowertigu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> scill' geb<hi rend="italic">ete</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis fornicetur cum uxore hominis tƿelfhindes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.1-3"/>, emendet ipsi marito hundtuelfti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.2-3"/> (centum uiginti) sol.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.3-3"/>; homini sixhindo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.4-3"/> hundteonti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.5-2"/> (C) solid.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.6-2"/>, cirlisco<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.7-2"/> XL<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.8-2"/> sol. emendetur.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_10.lnote.oe.9"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="70" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be hæmedðingum.] Gif mon hæme mid twelfhyndes monnes wife, hundtwelftig scill. gebete<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_10.attnote.fn.2"/> ðam were; syxhyndum men<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Af_10.attnote.fn.3"/> hundteontig scill. gebete; cierliscum men feowertig<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Af_10.attnote.fn.4"/> scill. gebete<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Af_10.attnote.fn.5"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="12" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="306" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XI} Gif mon hæme mid twelfhyndes monnes wife, hundtwelftig scill gebete ðam were; syxhundum men hundteontig scill gebete; cierliscum men feowertig scill gebete.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_10.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand Ehe bricht mit dem Weibe eines 1200-Mannes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_10.lnote.de.2"/>, so büsse er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_10.lnote.de.3"/> dem Manne 120<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_10.lnote.de.4"/> Schil.; einem 600-Manne büsse er 100<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_10.lnote.de.4"/> Schill.; einem gemeinfreien Manne büsse er 40<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_10.lnote.de.5"/> Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_10.lnote.de.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone commits adultery with the wife of a 1200-man, let him pay the husband 120 shillings; to a 600-man let him pay 100 shillings; to a common freeman let him pay 40 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="71" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone lies with the wife of a man whose wergeld is 1200 shillings, he shall pay 120 shillings compensation to the husband; to a husband whose wergeld is 600 shillings, he shall pay 100 shillings compensation; to a commoner he shall pay 40 shillings compensation [for a similar offence].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone lies with the wife of a man of a twelve-hundred wergild, he is to pay to the husband 120 shillings; to a man of a six-hundred wergild 100 shillings is to be paid; to a man of the <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> class 40 shillings is to be paid.<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_10.whinote.n.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="307" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a person has intercourse with the wife of a 1,200-man, let him pay 120 shillings to the husband; for a 600-man let him pay 100 shillings; for a man of <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> rank let him pay 40 shillings</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>cf. (wergeld enumerations)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_70">Ine 70</ref> <quote>Alfred enumerated the wergelds of the different ranks of West Saxon society five times as against Ine's once (n. 80)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_10">Abt 10–11</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_14">Abt 14</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_16">Abt 16</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_31">Abt 31</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_82">Abt 82–85</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="307"><ref target="clause:Af_11-2">Af 11.2</ref></note>
