        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> h. <hi rend="italic">Co; nur</hi> C <hi rend="italic">übrige; ausser</hi> CXX <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only h. Co; only C the others, except CXX R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">emendetur <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">emendetur added by Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyrl. <hi rend="italic">Hk T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyrl. Hk T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">LX <hi rend="italic">T Hk Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">LX T Hk Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">emendet <hi rend="italic">Brti; fehlt T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">emendet Brti; lacking in T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. aus</hi> -hundes</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered from -hundes</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Von Hurereien’ Rb B</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Of fornications’ Rb B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q behält Agsä. Endung bei. — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Wergeld 4ff., Stand 11, Thegn 13a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q retains the A.-S. ending. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Wergeld 4ff., Stand 11, Thegn 13a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Falls nicht im Ehebruch (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 8—9) ertappt und befehdet</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Unless caught in adultery (see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 8—9) and attacked in feud</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q Lond wieder dem Original näher</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q Lond again closer to the original</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nur spätere Q-Form liest <hi rend="italic">LX,</hi> was Schmid laut der Skala der Bussen der 3 Stände (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 21s. t; Ehebruch 9a; Eheschliessung 10) Af 18, 1 bevorzugt. Doch liegt dieser Fall oder Af 11, 2 nicht gleich. — Rosenthal (<hi rend="italic">Rechtsfolgen des Ehebruchs</hi> 70) meint, Ehe- und Verlöbnisbruch werde gleichmässig gestraft, was hieraus aber nicht zu folgern ist</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Only the later form of Q reads <hi rend="italic">LX,</hi> which Schmid prefers in accordance with the scale of compensations for the 3 ranks (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 21s. t; Ehebruch 9a; Eheschliessung 10) Af 18, 1. But neither the present case nor Af 11, 2 is parallel to that. — Rosenthal (<hi rend="italic">Rechtsfolgen des Ehebruchs</hi> 70) thinks that adultery and breach of betrothal were punished equally, which, however, cannot be inferred from this passage</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_10.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Gebot besonderer Zahlungsart (in Vieh, ohne Sklaven) bei anderer Unzuchtsbusse, das Af hinter 18, 1 setzt, stellt Ld, dem 18, 1 fehlt, hierher: bewusste Änderung, wohl 11. Jhs.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The provision prescribing a special mode of payment (in livestock, without slaves) for another compensation for unchastity, which Af places after 18, 1, is put here by Ld, which lacks 18, 1: a deliberate change, probably of the 11th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_10.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>gebete</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gebete</hi> (<hi rend="italic">man</hi>). H* &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_10.attnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>men</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">monnes wife</hi>. So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_10.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>feowertig</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">feowertigum</hi>. B &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_10.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>gebete</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">And þæt sy on cwycæhtum feogodum, ⁊ mon nænigne mon on þæt ne sylle</hi>; follows here in Ld instead of in cap. 18, § 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Af_10.whinote.n.1" n="1" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><label>paid</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Chap. 11 is concerned with compensations for assaults of various kinds and in various circumstances against women.</seg></note>
